{
  // T9 P-6 — Host face of the DSH dual-target convention
  // (`build:lib:host` + `build:lib:client`), adapted to our no-build reality.
  // DSH:  `tsc -b tsconfig.host.json && tsdown --env.DSH_BUILD_FACE host`
  // Ours: `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.host.json`
  //        (Node 24 type-stripping loads src/*.ts as source — T4 P-8.6 — and
  //        this workspace has no bundler, so the emit/tsdown halves are moot;
  //        the typecheck half is the whole guard).
  //
  // The host face is THE gate for a pure-host plugin: `lib` deliberately
  // EXCLUDES DOM, so any browser-only global (window/document/localStorage/…)
  // referenced in src/ fails this build. At the dsh host runtime those
  // globals are undefined, so this face pins the real invariant. The
  // repo-root tsconfig facade keeps TypeScript's default DOM lib on, which
  // is exactly why this face must be stricter than `pnpm typecheck`.
  //
  // Phase 5 (P5-T2): omo-team is host-only for the same reason as omo-agents,
  // omo-hooks and omo-commands — team formation and coordination semantics all
  // run in the Node process the agent lives in: members are created through
  // `ctx.subagents.startContinuable` (fork = (B), .omo/evidence/p5t1/FORK.md),
  // the vendored team-core state machine (types / member-parser / team-registry
  // / team-tasklist / team-state-store + closure) executes host-side, and the
  // tool layer's role gating / handshake state transitions are in-process
  // decisions. There is no browser half to type.
  //
  // The CLIENT FACE IS CONDITIONAL, and that is why this package ships only
  // this file: the visualization baseline (phase5-team.md §1 fork-(B) 终态 +
  // FORK.md §3.7) puts message visibility on the generic panels (subagentchat
  // + lead-session 'agent-message' frames, T10 assertions). A client face
  // exists ONLY if the T10 review rules that T11 (custom ChatNode fallback)
  // triggers — `ConversationNodeDefinition` + `ConversationEventRegistry.register`
  // would then land in `src/client/` WITH a `tsconfig.client.json`, and the
  // root `typecheck:libs` chain would grow the omo-agents-style conditional
  // (`if [ -d src/client ] …`) for this package. Until T10 says otherwise,
  // there is no src/client and no tsconfig.client.json — adding one now would
  // pre-empt a fork-adjacent ruling, which is a plan-level decision, not a
  // tsconfig edit. `typecheck:team` therefore runs THIS face only (see the
  // root package.json `typecheck:team` script).
  //
  // This is the FOURTH application of the P-6 host-face discipline after
  // omo-agents (Phase 2), omo-hooks (Phase 3) and omo-commands (Phase 4), not
  // an independent decision: the host-only reason is the same one in all four
  // packages, and so are the compilerOptions that express it (`lib: ["ES2022"]`
  // + `types: ["node"]` + `include: ["src"]` over the root tsconfig). Only the
  // two paragraphs above are package-specific. If this face ever needs to
  // diverge from the commands face, the divergence must be justified here —
  // not made silently by editing one of the files.
  "extends": "../../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
